#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/nn.rc -- Norwegian Nynorsk, the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "nn"`.
//
// Stage E109, group B: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block -- in the order of en.rc. An adaptation, not a letter-for-letter translation (owner's word
// 198.14); the glossary of the language is l10n/glossary/nn.tsv in the control contour.
// Keys stay in Latin letters as the hotkey field prints them (RULES 4). The quotation marks are
// « » and the dash is the spaced en dash of Norwegian (RULES 3). The tone is "du", as in the
// Windows interface in Nynorsk. The author's site is the English one: the feedback strings follow
// en.rc (GitHub Issues). Nynorsk is not Bokmål with other endings: the forms (eg, ikkje, kva,
// ein/ei/eit, -ar in the present) and some of the Windows terms (snøggtast, vegvisar, utsjånad,
// vindauge) are its own; the Bokmål file of the pair is nb.rc.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Norwegian Nynorsk -- `[general] language = "nn"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
